md('''## 8. Validation sequence and stop/go gates
| Phase | Artifact | Evidence to advance | Stop/revise trigger |
|---|---|---|---|
| A: business brief | One audience, problem, language, eligibility and cost/time ceiling | Owner decisions plus dated public problem evidence | Cannot define value, eligibility or acceptable work |
| B: private production proof | Three materially different original draft episodes | Actual local scripts, narration, visuals and renders; per-attempt timing, failures and rights | Cannot meet quality or budget without hidden labor |
| C: bounded audience pilot, separately authorized | Limited release set, hypothesis and fixed loss/time cap | Genuine audience response and platform compliance | No value signal, originality concerns or costs exceed cap |
| D: revenue viability | Observed eligible receipts and complete costs | Economic contribution supports continued investment | Only optimistic extrapolation or cash receipts confused with estimates |
| E: selective scale | Stable revisionable capabilities and exception queue | Measured quality maintained as volume grows | Volume reduces value or manual work grows faster than receipts |

Private milestone proposal: one 60–120 second episode first, then three distinct episodes if the first passes. This duration/sample size is a proposed engineering bound, not statistically sufficient market validation. Before any public pilot, fix numeric caps and analysis rules using owner constraints; they remain unknown here. No public release occurs in this research run.

| Check family | Proposed measurement | Interpretation |
|---|---|---|
| Technical | Full decode, audio/caption alignment, real stage timestamps, repeatability | Media correctness only |
| Editorial | Task demonstrably works, sourced claims, original explanation, reviewer corrections | Content utility candidate, not demand proof |
| Operational | Operator minutes, failed attempts, restart/cancel, support exceptions | Automation and recurring burden |
| Audience | Retention and useful response by topic/cohort; uncertainty and selection effects | Interest, not purchase or profit by itself |
| Commercial | Received cash, refunds/fees, owner time and economic cost | Business viability evidence, not universal performance |

Do not select only successful renders. Freeze records for every attempt and changed prompt/model. Separate exploration from later evaluation; record exposure to examples and avoid calling previously inspected samples held out.''')
md('''## 9. Risk register and unresolved decisions
| Risk | Consequence | Response / unresolved evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Repetitive mass-produced channel | Monetization rejection despite technically valid videos | Original substantive demonstration per episode and channel-level editorial review |
| Unsupported factual script | Audience harm and loss of trust | Claim/source mapping and genuine controlled demonstration |
| Model/voice/asset rights | Unusable commercial pipeline | Exact checkpoint and asset license register; no unauthorized voice cloning |
| Unmeasured local performance | Cost/throughput plan collapses | Measure sequential local stages before optional image/video generation |
| No eligible revenue route | No payable receipts | Confirm real account/country requirements; never infer from timezone |
| Hidden owner labor | Apparently positive cash, negative economics | Cost all review, maintenance, research and exceptions |
| Premature hierarchy | Diagram substitutes for implementation | Keep component references empty until verified; mark proposed units |
| Overfitting the pilot | Fragile apparent success | Diverse cases, recorded failures and later fresh evaluation |

**Owner decisions before implementation:** actual jurisdiction/payment eligibility; preferred language and audience; subject expertise; monthly cash and owner-time ceiling; acceptable synthetic voice/visual format; tolerance for written customer support; permission for a bounded private production pilot. These are not guessed from the user's device or location.

**Operating boundary:** no meetings is a design constraint; identity checks, written support, editorial decisions and exceptional issues cannot be promised away. Research completion is not permission to publish or spend.''')
md('''## 10. Results, defense and conclusion
**Completed:** parallel primary-source policy, business-model and local-stack research; current host inventory; a conditional seven-instance business architecture with shared planes, handoff contracts and Operations coordination; executed scenario arithmetic and fourteen focused checks (six economics checks and eight design-consistency/fault checks). **Not completed:** selected-niche demand validation, fresh local generation benchmark, account eligibility audit, audience release, sales or revenue observation.

The original ads-first suggestion is revised: advertising has relatively low fulfillment burden, but delayed eligibility makes it an option rather than a proven fastest-profit strategy. A practical original software-demonstration pilot is a tractable candidate because its factual value can be checked and expensive generated video is unnecessary. Candidate tools are not declared installed or production-ready. All seven instances and their internal layers remain proposed contracts, not deployed systems or automatically learned emergence. The economics worksheet remains illustrative ad-route arithmetic, not a complete seven-domain operating ledger. Domain costs must be consolidated once, with internal transfers excluded from revenue and no duplicated shared costs.

This plan can be rejected: if no narrow problem warrants original content, if local quality requires excessive manual correction, if rights or eligibility are unacceptable, or if realistic measured cost is unsupported by observed receipts, revise or stop. Negative evidence is a useful result. The next authorized decision should concern a bounded private proof, not an automated publishing factory.

### Research collaboration and disclosure
The initial three parallel research agents investigated platform policy, local production and business alternatives. Those source dossiers are retained. The multi-instance renovation is a coordinator-authored architectural revision, not a new external or independent review. The existing Langflow research collaborator was asked for a bounded critique without Paper 6 edits. The coordinator synthesized and checked arithmetic. The earlier internal final-review report applies to the single-instance revision; the current renovation has separate design-consistency and fault-injection checks, not external academic peer review. This is internal AI-assisted research, not external academic peer review. Sources establish their stated facts, not the success of this business. No study can promise significant earnings before evidence exists.''')
